# Bug: a list literal too wide for one line cannot be written at all.
#
# Written on one line, this list is 102 characters and the compiler refuses
# it as wider than 80. Written one element per line, as below, `kanso play`
# answers:
#   error[syntax]: expected an expression
#     --> b05_wide_list_literal.kso:14:22
#
# The same layout with a list that fits on one line is refused as "needless
# continuation: this statement fits on one line", which says the layout is
# the intended way to wrap a list. Expected: this file prints 2.
xs = [
  "the first sphere, at the origin, which is long enough to need wrapping"
  "the second sphere"
]
print "{length xs}"
